fido2ble (0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Stop reconnecting to devices that were unpaired or removed from BlueZ
    (closes: PoneBiometrics/fido2ble#33)
  * Always answer the host with a CTAPHID error when the BLE device cannot be
    connected or stops responding, so browsers no longer hang
    (closes: PoneBiometrics/fido2ble#34)
  * New options --connect-timeout, --response-timeout, --connect-attempts
  * Drop the PoneBiometrics apt source and signing key from the package
  * Build with pyproject.toml, run unit tests at build time

 -- Tobias Assarsson <tobias.assarsson@gmail.com>  Fri, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100

fido2ble (0.2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Added support for pairing while running
  * Added logging arguments for general log level and uhid log level
  * Improved disconnect and reconnect handling
  * Switched to adaptive characteristic paths
  * Added bluetooth address to hidraw device name

